# Environment files — catch-all (any .env anywhere in the tree). Specific
# entries below are kept for documentation of known locations.
.env
**/.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
docker-compose/.env
docker-compose/docker-compose.auth-volumes.yml
*.log
hs_err_pid*
# Build output only. A bare "META-INF/" also matches src/main/resources/META-INF,
# which silently swallowed every module's
# META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports
# — the file Spring Boot needs to register an auto-configuration. Modules that
# noticed worked around it with `git add -f`; jaiclaw-security did not, so its
# auto-config was absent from a fresh clone entirely.
target/**/META-INF/
maven-central-deploy/
op-vault/
docs/PRIVATE-DOCS-INDEX.md
/.claude/
/dependency-update-report.md
security-report-*.md
BUILD-MEMORY.md
feature-parity-report.md
**/feature-parity-report.md
/docs/dev/SUBSCRIPTION-PROVIDER-AUDIT-2026-06-15.md
# Internal compliance / risk audits — findings not for public consumption.
# The implementation PLANS they drive DO get committed; the raw AUDITS don't.
/docs/dev/COMPLIANCE-ANALYSIS-*.md

# Local marketing / non-framework scratch
docs-local/

# Frontend build artifacts (React SPAs — pipeline-studio, etc.)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
